# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
#
# config-check.baseline - release baseline for deploy/tools/config-check.sh (Z-INTAKE).
# Installed next to the checker (/usr/lib/candor/tools/, root 0644). Format: '|'-separated,
# first field = kind. Lines starting with '#' are comments.
#
#   unit|<unit>|<Section>|<Key>|<op>|<value>
#       effective directive of a unit after systemd merged fragment + all drop-ins.
#       op '=': exact; several '=' lines for one key = the exact assignment sequence, in order
#               (a drop-in that adds, resets or overrides anything changes the sequence).
#       op '~': ERE over the joined sequence (assignments joined with ' ;; '; an empty
#               assignment = reset = empty element; absent key = empty string).
#       op '*': value checked semantically by the checker (sealer SystemCallFilter: owned by
#               the sealer hardening work, AUD-RM2-SEA-06; allow-list mode + systemd-analyze
#               security deny-group items).
#       Any directive not listed for a unit (any section) is a FAIL.
#   sec|<unit>|<item>           systemd-analyze security items that may score > 0 (residuals
#                               documented in deploy/SPEC-NOTES.md D-21/D-25); any other FAILs.
#   nft-rule|<chain>|<json>     loaded rules of the release ruleset, in order (canonical JSON of
#                               the rule expressions; skuid as user name, counters without values)
#   nft-set|<name>|<json>       fixed sets (type, flags, elements)
#   tor|<Option>|=|<value>      the complete effective non-default option set (tor
#   tor|<Option>|int|<lo> <hi>  --dump-config short) with required values / tunable ranges
#   tor-full|<Option>|<value>   required values in --dump-config full (defaults and
#                               path-selection options)
#   tor-raw|<Option>            option names allowed in the torrc text (no abbreviations)
#   pg|<guc>|<b|s>|<value>      postgresql.conf, static (b = boolean, s = lower-case string)
#   pgc|<guc>|<value>           effective value printed by `postgres -C <guc>` (--host)
#   sysctl|<key>|<value>        kernel baseline (sysctl.d file, effective /proc/sys)
#   show|<kinds>|<Property>|<value>   `systemctl show` of the loaded unit (--host, live);
#                               kinds: comma list of all, tor, candor, pg
#
# Maintainers: `config-check.sh --emit-baseline --dir deploy/intake` prints the unit, nft and
# sec lines of a tree for review; '~'/'*' entries and the other kinds are maintained by hand.

